# TypeScript & React Standards

## General

- `strict: true` is enabled — no `any`, no type assertions without justification
- Prefer `unknown` over `any` when the type is genuinely unknown
- Remove unused variables and imports (enforced by `noUnusedLocals` / `noUnusedParameters`)

## Error Handling

Always surface errors to the user; never swallow them silently.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
async function load() {
  const data = await invoke('get_contexts');
  set({ contexts: data });
}

// ✅ GOOD
async function load() {
  try {
    const data = await invoke<Context[]>('get_contexts');
    set({ contexts: data });
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Failed to load contexts', err);
    // show toast or error state to the user
  }
}
```

## Zustand Stores

- One store per domain (`useContextStore`, `useConfigStore`)
- Keep stores flat; derive computed values with selectors
- Always handle errors in async actions — update an `error` field in state

## React Components

- Functional components only
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks (`src/hooks/`)
- Clean up `setTimeout` / `setInterval` in `useEffect` return functions

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — timer leak
useEffect(() => {
  setTimeout(() => save(), 500);
}, [value]);

// ✅ GOOD
useEffect(() => {
  const id = setTimeout(() => save(), 500);
  return () => clearTimeout(id);
}, [value]);
```

## Tauri IPC

- All `invoke()` calls live exclusively in `src/services/tauri.ts`
- Components and stores import from `tauri.ts`, never call `invoke()` directly
- Type the return value: `invoke<ReturnType>('command_name', { arg })`

## Dead Code

- Do not leave unused components, exports or API wrappers in the codebase
- Remove, don't comment out

## State Sync

When a store reloads data with the same selected ID, derived UI state (editors, forms) must react to the new content, not just the ID change.
